<!-- The test-only corner glyph (U+E000) of the test font, at 250 pixels with a black stroke of 16 pixels and a white fill, on white.
     Each of its four triangles has its apex at the bottom, and the glyph is moved 100 units right (its left edge), so the apexes
     lie at x = 8 + (x + 100) * 0.25 for the font-unit x of each apex: 45.5, 107, 193.5 and 258.5. The baseline is at 213
     (0.85 * 250 = 212.5, halves up), so the apexes lie 10 pixels above it, at y = 203. Half the stroke is 8 pixels.
     The first apex has an apex angle of 29.05 degrees and a mitre ratio of 3.987, below the limit of 4: its tip lies 8 * 3.987 = 31.9 pixels below its apex, at 234.9.
     The second has an apex angle of 28.87 degrees and a ratio of 4.012, past the limit: its bevel lies 8 / 4.012 = 1.99 pixels below its apex, at 205.0.
     The third has an apex angle of 20.05 degrees and a ratio of 5.745, past the limit: its bevel lies 8 / 5.745 = 1.39 pixels below its apex, at 204.39.
     The fourth has an apex angle of 40.27 degrees and a ratio of 2.905, below the limit: its tip lies 8 * 2.905 = 23.2 pixels below its apex, at 226.2.
     300 by 240 pixels, one frame. -->
<composition version="1" id="text-join-corner" width="300" height="240" fps="10" duration="1" background="#ffffff">
  <font src="fonts/framesmith-test-stroke-400.ttf" family="Framesmith Test Stroke"/>
  <text left="8" top="0" font-family="Framesmith Test Stroke" font-size="250" color="#ffffff" text-stroke="16px #000000">&#xE000;</text>
</composition>
